d by the defendant so i  definitely think it should be allowed  and i think the judge made the right  decision all right maybe it's the  defense attorney i mean but i tend to  disagree and dave i love asking a  prosecutor pro-defense question so here  it is i would argue that this  information about eastman threatening a  person  he isn't accused of a crime of doing is  more prejudicial than probative i  threaten this other guy that has nothing  to do with i do with my wife so how does  this come in  this is a tough one brian and terry's  got a good point because it could show  motive you have to establish that this  goes to motive because how else are you  going to show how why eastman kills  sessions why well he was this jealous  dude who was always lurking around and  exaggerating his relationship with frank  so  that's the argument now as a prosecutor  you have to be careful and i'm sorry to  equivocate on this because it is a close  call because if you admit this into  evidence and as a prosecutor if you  don't absolutely have to have this to  prove guilt  then you  could be overturned on appeal and that's  the last thing prosecutors want to do so  it's a close call some prosecutors would  be like hey let's take a step back not  use it because we got other good stuff  instead so it all depends on how  important this piece of evidence is to  make that decision whether to put it  into evidence i'm calling it now i'm  calling it a pellet argument we'll see  whether or not it actually works in the  long run well when we come back a group  of philadelphia teens wanted for murder  still ahead we take a closer look at  security camera footage showing the  children brutally beating an elderly man  to death  welcome back apparel brothers ages 10  and 14 years old turned themselves over  to philadelphia police as part of a  group who beat an elderly man to death  with a traffic cone police released  photos of the children involved and  video of the attack last week hopin